{"timestamp":1794625311,"method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"33333333-4444-4555-8666-777777777777","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"The cursor blinks like a patient lighthouse\non a black coast nobody else can see.\nYou type a name and the coast answers,\na path unspooling under your hands,\ndirectories opening the way rooms open\nwhen you already know which light switch works.\nThis is the oldest room in the new machine,\nolder than windows, older than the mouse\nthat taught the hand to point instead of speak.\nHere speech is exact. A missing letter\nis a closed door. A slash turned backward\nis a road that runs into the ditch.\nYou learn to mean what you say.\n\nThe prompt waits at the left margin,\na small stubborn animal that will not fetch\nuntil you finish the sentence.\nYou feed it flags, those short sharp sticks\nthrown ahead of the command,\nand it brings back lists, errors, silence,\nor the particular silence that means done.\nPipes run between processes\nthe way irrigation runs between fields:\none program's rain becomes the next field's drink,\nand nothing is wasted except the hours\nyou spend admiring the ditch.\nRedirection is a kind of mercy.\nSend the noise to a file. Send the file\nto tomorrow. Tomorrow will still be able to read.\n\nThere is a history here, arrowed upward,\nevery half-command you have ever mumbled,\nincluding the one you wish you had not.\nThere is a manual no one finishes,\nsectioned like a coastline into bays,\nand somewhere in it the flag you needed\nhas been waiting with monastic calm.\nYou grep the dark for a single string\nand the dark, obligingly, lights the matches,\neach one a small gold tooth in the coal.\nYou tail a log and the log keeps growing,\na river that refuses to arrive,\nand you sit with it the way people sit\nwith weather, learning which lines matter\nand which lines are only the machine\nclearing its throat.\n\nRemote, the same room opens\non a machine you will never touch.\nYour key is a file. Your presence\nis a session. If the wire fails,\nthe work can keep its own pulse\ninside a multiplexer, panes like cabin windows\non a ship that does not need you aboard\nto continue crossing. You detach.\nYou sleep. In the morning the tests\nare still running, or they are finished,\nor they have failed in a way that leaves\na precise paragraph explaining\nwhich assumption did not survive the night.\n\nThe beauty is not nostalgia.\nThe beauty is that a sentence can build a world,\nremove a world, move a world into another name,\nand then show you, in plain text,\nexactly what the world became.\nNo decoration. No fog.\nA line goes in, a line comes out,\nand between them the truth has to fit\nin the width of the glass you were given.\nWhen you are lost you ask where you are,\nand the shell, which has never once been kind\nand has never once been vague,\nprints the path back to you\nlike a street returned to its own map.\n\nClose the lid. The prompt remains,\nsomewhere, blinking, faithful as a pier light,\nholding your place in a language\nmade entirely of what happens next.\n\ndone"}},"_meta":{"totalTokens":20344,"requestTrimmedTokens":0,"eventId":"33333333-4444-4555-8666-777777777777-1292","agentTimestampMs":1794625311025,"promptId":"f22848f1-35cb-44d8-951d-9faa97985b39","streamStartMs":1794625289854,"turnStartMs":1794625288213,"updateType":"AgentMessageChunk","chunkId":647}}}
